The decisive issue is now clear: for the paper-native task “find any minimal dominating set,” a solver never needs to recover the plant. A greedy maximal independent set is already a minimal dominating set, and on factor input the same scan can be done before forming the product. I’m measuring that factor-aware route against the purported shortcut so the Track B rejection has concrete costs rather than merely saying “a polynomial algorithm exists.”
