A binary word of length L is a string of L zero/one bits. Its Hamming weight is
the number of 1 bits. The Hamming distance between two words is the number of
coordinates on which they differ. A constant-weight code of size k, weight w,
and minimum distance d is a set of exactly k distinct length-L words, every one
of weight w, such that every pair has Hamming distance at least d.

Choose a code from the candidate table below. Candidate IDs are 0-based. Your
code must contain the mandatory anchor ID 1. The answer is a strictly increasing
list of exactly 3 distinct IDs.

Parameters: L=9, k=3, w=3, d=6
Coordinate permutation: [8,5,3,6,0,7,2,1,4]

0: 016
1: 038
2: 043
3: 098
4: 0c1
5: 106
6: 1c0

Give the final JSON list inside <answer></answer> tags.
```

The answer is `<answer>[1, 4, 5]</answer>`.
`verify(inst, [1, 4, 5]) == (True, "ok")`, while
`verify(inst, [1, 4]) == (False, "wrong number of IDs: expected 3, got 2")`.
This smallest preset is hand-solvable: applying the nine-entry permutation to
the anchor twice identifies the other two words.

## Difficulty presets

| preset | cycle blocks `n` | code size | decoy orbits | word length | candidates | structured space |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| demo | 3 | 3 | 2 | 9 | 7 | 6 |
| easy | 8 | 5 | 12 | 40 | 53 | 91,390 |
| medium | 16 | 7 | 60 | 112 | 367 | 1,085,371,516,236 |
| hard (intended shipping) | 38 | 7 | 220 | 266 | 1,327 | 2,507,831,816,322,196 |

Easy was solved by one of three bare oracles. Medium and hard have no valid
oracle verdict because the API budget was exhausted during medium.

## Local gates

| gate | result | measurement |
|---|---|---|
| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted witnesses; orbit recovery matched each |
| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
| G3 | pass | tagged and fenced prose round-trip |
| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 structured guesses; space 2,507,831,816,322,196 |
| G5 | pass | demo has exactly 1/6 valid; strongest failing attack used 5,602,667 steps |
| G6 | pass | four attacks each 0/8; Algorithm X and orbit index each 8/8 |
| G7 | pass | doubled 532-bit instance verifies with the same 7-ID answer length |
| G8 | pass | 60/60 invariance and 60/60 carried-witness checks; 20/20 keys distinct |
| G9 | **pending** | size caps pass: 30 chars, 8 estimated tokens, 7 atoms, 294 operations |

## Partial bare oracle loop

| preset | seed | model | result | reason |
|---|---:|---|---|---|
| easy | 1900298301 | x-ai/grok-4.6 | solved | verified answer |
| easy | 1748461321 | anthropic/claude-sonnet-5 | failed | empty length-limited response |
| easy | 1599535317 | google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview | failed | submitted pair had distance 12 < 16 |
| medium | 1636691902 | x-ai/grok-4.6 | error | 900-second hard deadline |
| medium | three redraws | openai/gpt-5.6-terra | error | OpenRouter key total limit reached |

This is an incomplete infrastructure run, not a `hardened` or `too_easy`
verdict. No hinted or placebo arm was run, so `hinted_minus_placebo` is not yet
defined. After the key is replenished, rerun the bare ladder first, then run the
structural and placebo copies in separate directories as required by G9.

## Use

```python
import importlib.util

spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(
    "gen_1703_05171", "results/1703.05171/gen_1703_05171.py"
)
gen = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
spec.loader.exec_module(gen)

inst = gen.make_instance(seed=7, **gen.DIFFICULTY["demo"])
text = gen.render(inst)
candidate = gen.parse_answer("<answer>" + str(inst["answer"]) + "</answer>")
ok, reason = gen.verify(inst, candidate)
```

From the repository root, emission is:

```bash
bash scripts/emit.sh 1703.05171
```

Run that only after all oracle evidence exists and G9 passes.

## Caveats

The supplied permutation makes the family easy with hashing or text search;
that is the declared Track B reference algorithm. G4 is only a density estimate
under a prior that already includes the mandatory anchor and filters words that
visibly fail against it; it does not prove average-case hardness under other
priors. The attack panel does not include an ILP/CP solver, although it does
include the more directly relevant exact-cover Algorithm X and the strictly
faster construction-specific orbit algorithm. The canonical key is an
isomorphism-invariant color-refinement signature, not a complete canonical form
for arbitrary colored set systems. Most importantly, no shipping-level oracle
or G9 conclusion is available until the external API budget is restored.

